  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Split guarded direct-result lowering by authenticated call shape: fully proved calls retain an inlineable proved core, while selected residual-guard edges use a separately authorized general core with the same checked fallback. Dormant shapes are pruned. Stage H retained the Stage G 57-byte constprop core and added a 310-byte general core, but remained slower in timing.",
    "risks": [
      "The exact machine-code separation was measured with GCC on linux-x64; Clang and MSVC use portable no-inline attributes but were not measured in this lane.",
      "Stage H remained slower than Stage G: repeated measurements varied from about +1.0% to +5.9%, so this mechanism is negative performance evidence rather than an adoption recommendation.",
      "The full native suite has five unrelated stale IR-version assertions (actual 46, expected 45) in unclaimed FFI/exact-ownership tests; focused compiler, architecture, and strict-library validations pass."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "If adopted, update the Stage H experiment driver's structural expectations from one direct-result variant to the proved/general pair."
    ]
  }
